============================================================================================
DEMO 1 - cross-instance exactly-once (B3, wired VL-094):
  the gate PUSHES an admitted decision to instance A, which honors it and claims the
  decision_id in the SHARED Redis; the SAME decision presented to instance B (a separate
  process) is refused as a replay it never saw.
============================================================================================
instance A acted (push honored): 1
instance B verdict (same decision): (False, 'REF_VERIFY_REPLAY')
instance B acted: 0

CONCLUSION: cross-instance exactly-once holds over real cross-host TLS with a real shared Redis.
With a per-instance in-memory cache, instance B would have honored the decision a second time;
the shared store made the claim global. This is the gap VL-094 closes, proven live.

